ntent lives in the report: for top candidates, card fields (what-it-is / fit / recommendation+confidence / advantages / risks / provenance / effort) render as report items.\n- Recommendation is explicitly a non-authoritative suggestion, never a consensus verdict.\n- A `decisions` table (CC1 disposition declared + dry-run tested) records accept/decline/snooze and doubles as the label source feeding Wave 2's deferred weight-validation.\n- No Helping-Hand auto-plumbing yet; a future run wires accepts into Helping Hand and validation once accepted-decisions reach nâ‰¥30.\n\n**North-Star inclusion test (per-wave coverage)**\n- W1 Model surface â†’ NS1, NS2\n- W2 Collection fix â†’ NS1, NS4\n- W3 Benchmarks â†’ NS1, NS2, NS3 (fit)\n- W4 Awareness+value â†’ NS1, NS5\n- W5 Adoption (min) â†’ NS3, plus labelsâ†’NS4\n- W6 Map (deferred) â†’ only weak NS1\n\n**Stage 1 approval gate â€” decisions put to John**\n- Approve the resequenced 5-wave plan (yes / edit).\n- The map (W6): confirm defer (Shark Tank recommendation) or keep IN as a fenced optional final wave.\n- The adoption shrink: OK to not build Helping-Hand auto-adoption now and instead capture labels + log decisions until nâ‰¥30, then revisit later (yes / want more now).\n- Any reweighting of wave order.\n\n---\n\nNote: this summary is drawn from the anchors you supplied (the two member docs â€” the Stage 1 Master Plan and the Foreman-ready Implementation Plan). The git log shows W2â€“W5 have since been committed on this branch, so the plan above has largely been executed. Want me to reconcile these claims against the actual `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/` docs or the commits to flag any drift?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4422,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":29670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null